scope: |
  CORRECTING `room-post-names-its-claim`, released twenty minutes ago, which answered the wrong
  half of the owner's request.

  He asked for the claim slug to be reported TO HIM IN THE DIRECT CHAT — the CLI session — and said
  the room is fine too but secondary. I wrote the rule entirely under `## The rozum room`, so it
  reads as a room convention and says nothing about the channel he actually asked about. He had to
  come back and ask whether I had written it that way. I had not.

  WHY IT LANDED WRONG IS WORTH RECORDING: the room is where agents talk to agents, and I generalised
  "report who you are" into the coordination channel I had been using all session. The human's
  channel is the DIRECT chat, he cannot see the room while working, and the claim slug is what lets
  him tell one `claude-code` from another when several are running.

  THE FIX IS A PLACEMENT FIX, not a wording one. The rule comes out from under the room heading into
  its own block, with the direct chat named FIRST and the room named as the second channel, so
  neither reads as the whole rule.

  ALSO the `multi-agent` plugin, whose step 5 currently says "announce it in the coordination room"
  — same one-sided shape, same fix. `.agents/plugins` is in `paths` because the pointer is a
  DISTINCT tracked path from the files inside the submodule; the guard taught me that an hour ago.
next: move the block, name the direct chat first, bump the plugin
